        "title": "feat: support signed ClawHub default feed",
        "body": "## Summary\n- add the bundled ClawHub feed trust-root slot used by the built-in `clawhub-public` marketplace profile\n- keep `OPENCLAW_CLAWHUB_FEED_TRUSTED_KEY_ID` / `OPENCLAW_CLAWHUB_FEED_TRUSTED_PUBLIC_KEY` as development, private deployment, rotation, and emergency override paths\n- document the ClawHub private-signing-key vs OpenClaw public-verification-key split, including that OpenClaw must not bootstrap trust from a ClawHub `/public-key` endpoint\n\n## Stack\n- depends on the approved hosted feed trust stack through #98350\n- pairs with the ClawHub signing PR: https://github.com/openclaw/clawhub/pull/3005\n- RFC direction updated in https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/25\n\n## Validation\n- Follow-up bundled-root update: `git diff --check`\n- Earlier branch validation before the bundled-root wording update:\n  - `node scripts\\run-vitest.mjs src\\plugins\\official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts src\\plugins\\official-external-plugin-catalog-envelope.test.ts`\n  - `pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts docs/cli/plugins.md`\n  - `pnpm tsgo:core:test`\n\n## Notes\n- This PR intentionally does not invent or hardcode a fake production ClawHub public key. Once ClawHub generates the production Ed25519 feed-signing keypair, only the public key/key id should be added to `DEFAULT_OFFICIAL_EXTERNAL_PLUGIN_CATALOG_CLAWHUB_TRUSTED_KEYS`; the private key stays in ClawHub deployment secret storage.\n- Env/config trust roots remain supported for development, private ClawHub deployments, dual-key rotation windows, threshold changes, and emergency root replacement.\n- The current sparse worktree does not have a package root, so the follow-up `oxfmt` rerun was not available there.",
